{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cevmghb5q1FRw96uknENo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The three failures were a real bug in the PDF background-image feature, not flaky tests, so I fixed the root cause instead of deleting coverage:\n\n- **Bug**: `xhtml2pdf/xhtml2pdf_reportlab.py` tracked \"have I drawn this template's background yet\" with a list (`backgroundids`) that was never cleared, and only recorded an entry when a template *had* a background. This meant (a) a background never got re-applied if its template was revisited later in the document, and (b) a template switch to a template *without* a background left no boundary marker, so the previous background kept bleeding onto later pages. It also meant a multi-pass TOC build (`multiBuild`) accumulated stale page-number bookkeeping from earlier passes.\n- **Fix**: register a boundary every time the active page template *changes* (not just the first time it's seen), including a `None` marker for backgroundless templates, and reset this state at the start of every build pass via a new `handle_documentBegin` override. Updated `watermarks.py`'s range logic to skip merging on `None` markers while still using them as range boundaries.\n\nFull suite: 173 passed, 2 skipped (pre-existing, unrelated), 0 failed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":315,"cache_read_input_tokens":68447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":315},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0ef49aa-836b-472f-890c-6d99d5245934","uuid":"b26baaa9-126b-4759-927d-23c9641f156c","timestamp":"2026-09-11T01:18:31.993Z","request_id":"req_011Cevmgh7ZTzBJJ4VDLFkX6"}
